slither-report.json
slither-report.sarif

# Repo root clutter — images + personal files
# (allow frontend/public/ and frontend/src/assets/ images)
/*.jpg
/*.jpeg
/*.png
/*.gif
/*.bmp
/*.xlsx
/*.avif
/*.webp
CODEBASE_FULL.txt
CODEBASE_OVERVIEW.txt

# Audit artifacts are EXPLICITLY tracked — every security review belongs on GitHub.
# Prior versions of this file ignored `SECURITY_AUDIT_*.md`, `findings_*.txt`, and
# `/*.docx` which silently dropped post-rule audits from version control
# (caught SECURITY_AUDIT_300_AGENT.md, the canonical reference). Keep these files
# in tree. If a genuine scratch / working buffer needs to stay out, prefix with
# a leading dot (e.g. `.audit_findings.md`, `.spartan_unpacked/`) which is
# already covered by general dotfile conventions.
# Do NOT add SECURITY_AUDIT_*.md / findings_*.txt / tegridy_*.docx back to ignore.

# FRESH-EYES L-1: catch-all for secrets in any subdir
**/.env
**/.env.*.local
**/.env.local
**/keystore/
**/*.key
**/wallet.json

# ── Stray artefacts and audit scratch (added 2026-08-15) ────────────────────
# Ignored, NOT deleted. Each was sitting untracked at the repo root where a
# `git clean -fd` would take it along with anything real beside it — which has
# already cost this repo twice (WORKORDER_V2.md and
# scripts/verify-program-constants.mjs were both real work found untracked).
# Ignoring them means the next `git status` shows only things that matter.
nul
tl.so
idx.html
*.mp4
.spartan_unpacked/
.audit_diffs/
.audit_2026_freshlook/

# Playwright HTML report (generated per run)
frontend/playwright-report/
